%% M2 key flow 2: parcel-service validates an issued quote before booking.
%% GET /api/v1/pricing/quotes/{quoteId} - requires a bearer token.
%% The reply is built from the stored snapshot only. An expired quote and an
%% unknown id get the same 404.
%% Simplified for the design report: one alt covers both failure cases.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as parcel-service
    participant GW as api-gateway
    participant PS as pricing-service
    participant RD as Redis

    Note over P: the booking request carries the<br/>quoteId the customer was shown
    P->>GW: GET /api/v1/pricing/quotes/{quoteId}<br/>Authorization: Bearer ...
    GW->>PS: validate the token,<br/>then forward
    PS->>RD: findById(quoteId)
    RD-->>PS: snapshot, or empty
    alt found and still valid
        PS-->>P: 200: the stored snapshot, verbatim<br/>(fee, breakdown, zones, expiresAt)
    else unknown id, or expired
        PS-->>P: 404 problem+json<br/>QUOTE_NOT_FOUND
    end
    Note over GW,PS: expired and unknown give the same answer,<br/>so expiry cannot be probed
